From: Florian Kleber <26285351+kleberbaum@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 08:28:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] docs(okf): record the store and the permissions in golem
 run

The wiki says that golem run opens no store and hands the plugins no
permissions, the notebooks of the testing page ask the old questions,
and the answers that the agent gave its own questions on the way are
recorded nowhere, so a reader would take the state of the tree from
pages that no longer hold.

The index, the README and the testing page now name what golem run
does with the store and the permissions and what the notebooks hold of
it. The log records the change. The open items drop what is built and
name what stays open, the members of the group admin, the flag of
getOfflinePermission that the native lacks, the resend of the command
tree, the budget of a command of LuckPerms and two quirks of LuckPerms
that wait for their issues. The API page says what of its section 16
is built and where it differs, and the answers of the agents hold
every choice of this work.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016dYAZEa3eZnoeGd1c8FkBT
