+The handler of the PermissionAPI and the check of a sender are built: the plugin
+`golem-permissions` of the runtime answers the PermissionAPI with `Permissions::has_permission`,
+and `Context::has_permission` and `Context::check_permission` answer what
+`Permissible.hasPermission(name:)` and `isPermissionSet(name:)` answer, the second as the field
+`set` of `PermissionAnswer`, see [Permissions](plugins/permissions.md#the-check-of-a-sender). They
+differ from section 9.9 in two points. A source without a profile holds every node from the level
+2 and none below it, the default `OP` of the table above, but a player gets no default of a plugin
+and no default `OP` for an operator, since no plugin declares its permissions to the runtime yet,
+so a node that no rule decides is not held. And the tables are not rebuilt on every change: a
+command of the port of LuckPerms installs its change at once, while a change that another writer
+puts into the store reaches the checks once the next tick woke the reload of the resolver.
+
 The first area writes these as the first entries of the mapping and of `api/golem-own.toml`, and
 `golem_bridge::Game` and `Context::game()` become a shim over `golem-client`, so `golem-essentials`,
 `golem-essentials-spawn` and the notebooks `04_plugins`, `05_bridge_build` and `07_forge_boot` keep
