+  deletes, unless the command ends in `--update-parent-lists`, so a group created later under the
+  same name gives the old members their group back (`DeleteGroup.java` lines 108 to 124 of
+  LuckPerms 5.5.71). `commands-allow-op: true` of the `config.yml` of LuckPerms (line 637), which
+  `LPBukkitPlugin.java` registers as the default `OP` of every node of the commands (lines 261 to
+  266), gives every operator of any level every command of LuckPerms, `/lp user <name> permission
+  set * true` included. The port removes the group from every member and grants the commands to
+  the group `admin` alone. Both are quirks for an issue each, which section 6 of CONTRIBUTING.md
+  asks for, and wait for their numbers on [Permissions](plugins/permissions.md).
 - `/golem status` does not name the permission handler that Forge took, issue
   [#141](https://github.com/skytekx/golem/issues/141). The warning that the mod logs on
   `ServerStartingEvent` when Forge takes another handler than `golem:permissions` is the only sign.
